complete evidence","sha256":"db6c79006b52e76d07575f6da52e35dbc34386087b91c3c8a0b6ca39b6814ed0"},"fragments":{"reason":"30 KB startup budget; follow record pointers for complete evidence","sha256":"d085d9a0c5116d418e215eba9c920e0f2f5b2da5feba967033cf77038423bdee"},"later_events":{"reason":"30 KB startup budget; follow record pointers for complete evidence","sha256":"eb4c62a5f4340a9d3f03a3c295f5533962a7741e0af3a14deced49db57f8af61"}},"readiness":{"blockers":"CLAIM_INCOMPLETE:clause_inventory|CLAIM_INCOMPLETE:ending_or_current_basis|CLAIM_INCOMPLETE:savings_residuals","claim_present":"yes","claim_record_errors":"unresolved_material_gaps","decision_origin":"inherited_legacy_v2","exhausted_steps":"","instrument_id":"EO:13472","provisional_status":"yes","ready_for_human_review":"no","ready_tier":"","step_clause_inventory":"open","step_counterevidence":"done","step_ending_or_current_basis":"open","step_opus_media":"n/a","step_original_text":"done","step_provisional_status":"done","step_savings_residuals":"open","step_shared_sources":"n/a","steps_applicable":"6","steps_done":"3"},"readiness_blockers":[{"step":"ending_or_current_basis","what":"no current-law lead is checked through 2026-10-14 (U.S. Code entries are current only through 2026-10-09); confirm the last days by hand"}],"schema":"eo-case-bundle/v1","status":"yes","text_pointers":[{"first_1500_characters":"By the authority vested in me as President by the Constitution and the laws of the United States of America, it is hereby ordered as follows:\n\nSection 1. Policy. It is the policy of the Federal Government to ensure that each executive branch agency can perform its essential functions and remain an effectively functioning part of the Federal Government under all conditions. Accordingly, each agency shall take all appropriate actions to establish, maintain, and, as necessary, revise an order of succession, or to propose presidential action to establish or revise an order of succession.\n\nSec. 2. Definitions. As used in this order:\n\n(a) \"agency\" means:\n\n (i)          an executive agency as defined in section 105 of title 5, United States Code, other than the Government Accountability Office; and\n\n (ii)          the United States Postal Service and the Postal Regulatory Commission; and\n\n(b) \"order of succession\" means a list of officials by position who shall act as and perform the functions and duties of the office of the head of the agency in the event that the office-holder has died, resigned, or otherwise become unable to perform the functions and duties of the office. \"Order of succession\" does not include any order, rule, memorandum, or other document delegating or partially delegating the authority of an office.\n\nSec. 3. Orders of Succession Requiring Presidential Action.\n\n(a) Each agency for which presidential action is required to establish an order of succession shall dr","path":"jobs/app-executive-orders/output/texts/executive-order-13472-executive-branch-responsibilities-with-respect-orders-succession.txt","sha256":"bb25d77d33612dd42a8e2d9e51aa2d2d54c26dfe24a557915fdf77d279a5ab1c","source":{"line":3512,"path":"jobs/app-transcriptions/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"c5ca57f7ceb3b3d71e90c6aade50c6117816c64e7c1bbe8da1ca973ff2197a90"}},{"first_1500_characters":"Executive Order 13472 of September 11, 2008 \nExecutive Branch Responsibilities With Respect To Orders of \nSuccession \nBy the authority vested in me as President by the Constitution and the \nlaws of the United States of America, it is hereby ordered as follows: \nSection 1. Policy. It is the policy of the Federal Government to ensure \nthat each executive branch agency can perform its essential functions and \nremain an effectively functioning part of the Federal Government under \nall conditions. Accordingly, each agency shall take all appropriate actions \nto establish, maintain, and, as necessary, revise an order of succession, \nor to propose presidential action to establish or revise an order of succession. \nSec. 2. Definitions. As used in this order: \n(a) ‘‘agency’’ means: \n(i) an executive agency as defined in section 105 of title 5, United \nStates Code, other than the Government Accountability Office; and \n(ii) the United States Postal Service and the Postal Regulatory Com-\nmission; and \n(b) ‘‘order of succession’’ means a list of officials by position who shall \nact as and perform the functions and duties of the office of the head \nof the agency in the event that the office-holder has died, resigned, or \notherwise become unable to perform the functions and duties of the office. \n‘‘Order of succession’’ does not include any order, rule, memorandum, \nor other document delegating or partially delegating the authority of an \noffice. \nSec. 3. Orders of Succession Requiring Presi","path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/texts/cd-job-fr-originals-13472-f6144cf3f4.txt","sha256":"74605ddf2ecb12ca4c3b9f0f1f8c56f7287c9aa1b7f10daf32851d7aba60ac95","source":{"line":8799,"path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"2056127d0ba31a362bc11598ceaafb4be95f3fd40e9ee59a0d0e104d2e446401"}},{"first_1500_characters":"{\"member\": \"usc02.xml\", \"note_id\": \"iddcb8117d-3a6e-11f1-a0f3-db3efcbbb4ee\", \"citation\": \"2 U.S.C. 685 note\", \"heading\": \"Ex. Ord. No. 11845. Delegation of Certain Reporting Functions to Director of Office of Management and Budget\", \"subjects\": [\"11845\"], \"status_line\": \"Ex. Ord. No. 11845, Mar. 24, 1975, 40 F.R. 13299, as amended by Ex. Ord. No. 12608, Sept. 9, 1987, 52 F.R. 34617, provided:\", \"text\": \"Ex. Ord. No. 11845. Delegation of Certain Reporting Functions to Director of Office of Management and Budget\\nEx. Ord. No. 11845, Mar. 24, 1975, 40 F.R. 13299, as amended by Ex. Ord. No. 12608, Sept. 9, 1987, 52 F.R. 34617, provided:\\nBy virtue of the authority vested in me by the Impoundment Control Act of 1974 (Public Law 93–344; 88 Stat. 332, (2 U.S.C. 681 et seq.), hereinafter referred to as the Act) [subchapters I and II of this chapter], and section 301 of title 3 of the United States Code, the Director of the Office of Management and Budget is hereby designated and empowered to exercise, as of October 1, 1974 without ratification or other action of the President (1) the functions required by sections 1014(b) and 1014(d) of the Act [subsecs. (b) and (d) of this section] of transmitting to the Comptroller General of the United States and to the Office of the Federal Register copies of special messages transmitted pursuant to section 1012 or 1013 (2 U.S.C. 683 and 684) of the Act; and (2) the function conferred upon the President by section 1014(e) of the Act (2 U.S.C. 685","path":"jobs/current-law/output/USC_EO_NOTES.jsonl","sha256":"ac1e287b6b606b8adc5c1975f662aae2d31989c1d072e32c89dbc38f6efe8016","source":{"line":3,"path":"jobs/current-law/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"5b6e5de61be4ea9c9c4749827c02d0c9d484107505b7e9adae3172a42351c188"}},{"first_1500_characters":"Instrument: EO:13472\nSource: https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2008-09-15/pdf/E8-21651.pdf\nSHA-256 of the downloaded file: f6144cf3f45643b616e1d68d492f58c73976e1e8819f4a1010e641955fef860c\nLocation: 73 FR 53353, PDF pages 1-2 (confidence high)\nMachine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors and parts of neighbouring documents on the same pages. Not an authenticated transcription: check the PDF pages.\n\n=== PDF page 1 of 2 ===\nPresidential Documents\n53353 \nFederal Register \nVol. 73, No. 179 \nMonday, September 15, 2008 \nTitle 3— \nThe President \nExecutive Order 13472 of September 11, 2008 \nExecutive Branch Responsibilities With Respect To Orders of \nSuccession \nBy the authority vested in me as President by the Constitution and the \nlaws of the United States of America, it is hereby ordered as follows: \nSection 1. Policy. It is the policy of the Federal Government to ensure \nthat each executive branch agency can perform its essential functions and \nremain an effectively functioning part of the Federal Government under \nall conditions. Accordingly, each agency shall take all appropriate actions \nto establish, maintain, and, as necessary, revise an order of succession, \nor to propose presidential action to establish or revise an order of succession. \nSec. 2. Definitions. As used in this order: \n(a) ‘‘agency’’ means: \n(i) an executive agency as defined in section 105 of title 5, United \nStates Code, other than the Governm","path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/texts/EO_13472.txt","sha256":"7ec7a71ee81f779b5e8a468a3cffd12987b3d22f859ef8bb04eaeca183ffcfd7","source":{"line":2122,"path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"8fc972513c9b537637c38f2360148db27aedc032140a7315471e2ef03fc7b4d3"}},{"first_1500_characters":"Wanted: queue:EO:13472:5USC3345etseq;EO13472,11030\nCited by: EO:13472\nSource: https://web.archive.org/web/20260711014000id_/https://www.congress.gov/public-laws/119th-congress\nSHA-256 of the downloaded file: d1248a4f6cfd1bff5918190a2335b3cddc5b90718574ae34890d6d77f6ce8231\nLocation: 5USC3345etseq;EO13472,11030\nMachine-extracted text (from a scan's text layer for older documents). Not an authenticated transcription; check the PDF.\n\n�\b\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000��}�r�H���|\u0005�sN�\u001dAJ��t�ڠ(Y\u0017�vH�}z.�(\u0012%�,\u0010`\u0017\u0000��l�<����y�\u001f�̬\u0002\bR E�`��]9¶\u0004���UYy�̬����{��ա5\u000e'�ޟ����eA����/A�r�7zW�^\u0001?�����\u0005ކ\"t��U4p��:c�������$\u000f���\u0007����drf�7�'ow���\u0018\u0013\u001e2�\u001cNK��Hܽ+�k!����l� �P���\u0010��.���5\u001c3\u0019������K�Bz\u001c�M���3�\u0019�w\\�Qz�r�Y-M\u0001\u0001�-�K�č�2�5D-x��{\u000f��i۝\u0012�%\u0017��-���\u0014�=:�a��\u0012�F��J1\u001a�A��k��\u0012�5B�� <��}y��� \u001a|��0��3>\u0012��Bqǭ\u0003\u0016�M��]K���՜X8'�_��O}!�;+���\u0005nL��m��=\u001fLq�3���P�)�4_�n`1ϱ��\u0002&\u0019���\b_\n�p�Bk�`\n\u0007�{\u0016��0�\u0005��Hq�\u001a̬9=�\u0017M\u0006\\�Xɞ�